  "summary": "Proves the Multiplicity-Carrier Decoupling Trilemma for non-abelian coset states: (1) Commutant measurements have identically zero mutual information (I = 0.0 bits) with any hidden conjugacy element by Schur invariance. (2) Carrier recoupling across k >= 3 copies is strictly non-commuting: [K_12, K_23]_{(0,0,0),(0,0,1)} = n for all n >= 3, ruling out simultaneous diagonalization. (3) Transforming carrier parenthesizations requires Racah 6j associators acting on a multiplicity space of factorial dimension dim(Commutant) = 2^Omega(n log n).",
