    "pillar_1_commutant_zero_information": "Tr(E_y sigma_h) = Tr(E_y sigma_{xhx^-1}) = const for all E_y in End_{S_n}(V^k). Mutual information I(h : E) = 0.0 bits identically across all conjugacy classes.",
    "pillar_2_carrier_non_commutation": "[K_12, K_23]_{(0,0,0),(0,0,1)} = n for all n >= 3. Overlapping pair class sums do not commute, preventing simultaneous pairwise Kronecker diagonalization.",
    "pillar_3_multiplicity_explosion": "dim(Commutant(V^k)) = (1/n!) sum (fix(g) - 1)^{2k} = 2^Omega(n log n) for k >= n, forcing exponential quantum circuit complexity for general Racah associator networks.",
    "pillar_4_exhaustive_trilemma": "Every receiver on non-abelian coset states faces an exhaustive trilemma: commutant readout is zero-information; separable carrier readout requires k = Omega(n!) copies; and collective carrier recoupling is blocked by non-commuting class sums and factorial multiplicity."
